CUDA & NPP Batch Image Processor - Installation Guide

Requirements:
- NVIDIA GPU with CUDA support
- NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit (including nvcc, cudart, nppif, and nppc)
- GNU Make and a bash-compatible shell (for run.sh)

Linux / CUDA Lab Environment:
1. Clone the repository:
   git clone https://github.com/LoshiniRP/Cuda-NPP-Batch-Processor.git
   cd Cuda-NPP-Batch-Processor
2. Build and run:
   chmod +x run.sh
   ./run.sh

Windows (with CUDA Toolkit installed):
1. Open Developer Command Prompt or a shell where nvcc is in PATH.
2. Compile with nvcc linking cudart, nppif, and nppc.